WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.000
Now the bad day.

2
00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.800
You open a hatch and see water over the floorboards.

3
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:07.875
Work in this order.

4
00:00:08.125 --> 00:00:10.125
First, find the source.

5
00:00:10.375 --> 00:00:14.575
Check the through-hulls, the hoses, the shaft seal, and the hull itself.

6
00:00:14.825 --> 00:00:17.125
Second, stop it or slow it.

7
00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:19.200
Close the seacock.

8
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:22.550
Drive a soft wood plug into a failed fitting.

9
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.600
Stuff a cushion or rags into a hole.

10
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:32.400
Here’s a tip worth more than any pump: tie a plug beside every through-hull now, so it’s there when you need it.

11
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:36.350
Third, pump, with everything you have, buckets included.

12
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.850
Fourth, call for help early.

13
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:43.150
A pan-pan if you’re holding your own, a Mayday if you’re sinking.

14
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.975
Why early?

15
00:00:45.975 --> 00:00:49.900
Because the radio stops working when the batteries go under.

16
00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.675
And get life jackets on everyone.

17
00:00:52.925 --> 00:00:57.000
If the leak is winning and shallow water is close, head for it.
